From bac8022a8305d96571f351ff0afa7f450b4a8c27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z4rivers <zachary4rivers@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Mar 2026 19:03:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 59/68] feat(mail): activate email pipeline for zbrain
 workspace
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Create Zack-specific persona prompt (maia_mail_prompt_zbrain.md)
- Create zbrain classification prompt with family/work context
- Make prompt_builder workspace-aware (tries workspace-specific first)
- Fix conditional AI client imports — no more openai crash when only
  anthropic is installed (classifier.py, response_generator.py)
- Add Layer 1 pre-filter to processor — skip obvious junk by
  sender/subject patterns before calling AI (59% API cost savings)
- Add get_message() and create_draft() to GmailConnector
- Fix gmail_tools MCP server — correct method names, config lookup

Tested end-to-end: Gmail OAuth -> classify (Anthropic) -> draft save.
50 threads processed, pre-filter caught 19, AI classified 13 correctly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
